Keep @github/copilot's sdk/index.js in the built-in copilot extension.

Upstream strips it because desktop VS Code restores platform-specific SDK
files at packaging time and the file is dead weight in the VSIX they ship.
This build has no such later stage for the extension host side: the file is
what the package.json exports map points at ("./sdk" -> "./sdk/index.js",
written by the extension's postinstall), and it is the version-matched SDK
entry the extension resolves when no platform package matches at runtime.
Without it the copilotcli session provider dies with "Cannot find module
.../@github/copilot/sdk/index.js" on device, three renames away from the
line removed here.

The SDK entry is plain JavaScript (its native-addon lookups key off
os.type(), which reports "Linux" on Android, and are lazy per addon), so
shipping it costs 2.6 MB and unlocks the whole session path.

--- a/build/.moduleignore
+++ b/build/.moduleignore
@@ -222,7 +222,6 @@
 @xterm/xterm-addon-*/out-test/**

 # @github/copilot - strip unneeded binaries and files
-@github/copilot/sdk/index.js
 @github/copilot/prebuilds/**
 @github/copilot/clipboard/**
 @github/copilot/ripgrep/**
